WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.549
For more than a decade, the Tesseract has
been a crucial force behind the actions and

00:00:04.549 --> 00:00:08.180
motivations of many of the Marvel Cinematic
Universe's major players.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.640
Let's take a look at some of the lesser-known
or little-remembered facts about the origins,

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.720
powers and timeline of the story thread which
has bound the Marvel movies together.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.120
The Tesseract traces its origins as far back
as time itself.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:26.400
In the MCU, the Big Bang brought about six
primal elemental singularities: Time, Reality,

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.780
Soul, Mind, Power, and Space.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:34.940
“One down, five to go.”

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.540
The essence of the universe itself was forged
by mysterious cosmic beings into the Infinity

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.040
Stones.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.600
The Space Stone came into the possession of
several ancient civilizations, including the

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.180
Celestials.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:50.880
At some point, its power was harnessed by
a crystalline cube casing : the Tesseract.

00:00:50.899 --> 00:00:54.969
The origin of the cube has yet to be revealed,
but its purpose was to tame the raw power

00:00:54.969 --> 00:00:57.820
of the Space Stone, making it more easily
controllable.

00:00:57.969 --> 00:01:01.999
At some point, Odin, the ruler of Asgard,
came into possession of the Tesseract and

00:01:01.999 --> 00:01:06.110
housed it in his own vault, as the crown jewel
of his collection of some of the most powerful

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:08.830
cosmic weapons and artifacts in the universe.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:12.920
Odin captured and stored in his heavily guarded
vault any weapon or relic he thought could

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:17.830
possibly bring about end times also known
as Ragnarok and the Tesseract definitely fit

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:18.340
that bill.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:24.060
In The First Avenger, Captain America fights
the Hydra super-soldier Red Skull aboard the

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.060
airship Valkyrie during the film's climactic
battle.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:31.560
As the Valkyrie speeds toward New York City
armed with nuclear warheads, the Red Skull

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:36.439
attempts to turn the tables on Cap by barehanding
the Tesseract but it doesn't exactly go well

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:36.940
for him.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:41.479
A portal opens, blasting Red Skull out of
the ship and carrying him off to parts unknown,

00:01:41.479 --> 00:01:45.310
while the Tesseract burns through the hull
of the Valkyrie and descends into the depths

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:46.020
of the ocean.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.920
Poor Steve Rogers isn't far behind, as the
entire airship plunges into the icy water,

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:54.260
where Captain America would remain frozen
for the next 70 years.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.399
“Is there anything else about the Tesseract
that we ought to know now?”

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.640
“You should’ve left it in the ocean.”

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:04.159
It was nearly a decade before Red Skull appeared
in another MCU movie.

00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:08.330
In his Infinity War cameo, the character is
portrayed by Ross Marquand of The Walking

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:11.320
Dead fame, replacing The First Avenger's Hugo
Weaving.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.720
During the film, it’s revealed that the
Space Stone transported Red Skull to Vormir

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.280
and somehow imprisoned him there.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.590
The Red Skull explains that his quest to control
an Infinity Stone led it to reject him.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:25.590
He's now intrinsically linked to the Soul
Stone, as its guardian, but is never able

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:26.600
to possess it.

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:32.260
Sometime after Cap's fateful battle with the
Red Skull, a deep sea expedition led by Howard

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:36.710
Stark recovered the Tesseract in the cold
waters of the Arctic Ocean, while searching

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:38.140
for the body of Steve Rogers.

00:02:38.209 --> 00:02:42.680
The brilliant inventor had been instrumental
in creating the scientific process that transformed

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.660
Rogers from a scrawny weakling into a super
soldier.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:49.940
While in possession of the Tesseract, Stark
researched and studied its nature.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:54.599
The Tesseract's official first onscreen appearance
comes in a stinger following 2011’s Thor,

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:58.720
but the MCU’s first Tesseract reference
is actually in Iron Man 2.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.640
During a scene in which Howard's son Tony
is flipping through his father's notebook,

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.740
the audience is able to catch a glimpse of
a drawing of the Tesseract.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:11.440
Project PEGASUS was formed in the 1980s as
a joint operation between the United States

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:15.800
Air Force and NASA, once the Tesseract came
into possession of the U.S. government.

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:19.840
The project had been mentioned in other MCU
films, but Captain Marvel was the first to

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.879
shed more light on the top secret undertaking.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:26.920
Mar-Vell, a Kree scientist posing as human
Dr. Wendy Lawson on Earth, is able to obtain

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:31.730
access to the Tesseract and attempts to harness
its power to produce a lightspeed engine.

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:35.840
When a test fighter flown by Carol Danvers
and Lawson is shot down by Kree Starforce,

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:40.500
Danvers destroys the powerful engine and,
in the process, absorbs the cosmic power of

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:41.500
the Space Stone.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:47.840
In Captain Marvel, Carol Danvers gains full
control of her powers and memories in 1995,

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.220
six years after her crash and subsequent abduction
by the Kree.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:54.870
She's then able to thwart her pursuers and
uncover the Tesseract in the hidden space

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:56.460
station in Earth's near orbit.

00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:01.440
Once recovered, the Tesseract is kept safe
by Mar-Vell's beloved pet "cat," Goose.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.629
Of course, Goose is actually a cat-shaped
Flerken who stores the artifact in a pocket

00:04:05.629 --> 00:04:07.000
dimension in her stomach.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:11.599
Flerkens just so happen to resemble Earthly
felines in many ways, except for the many

00:04:11.599 --> 00:04:14.020
toothy tentacles they can release from their
mouth.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:18.750
The tentacles enable the deceptively deadly
Flerken to devour large prey or objects to

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:21.380
teleport or store in stomach lining pocket
dimensions.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:26.440
Later, Goose horks up the Tesseract onto Nick
Fury's desk, and Project PEGASUS is revived

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.940
to further study the object.

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:33.720
It is soon relocated to a SHIELD facility
in the Mojave Desert to unlock its full capabilities.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:38.360
The Tesseract has appeared in at least 10
Marvel Cinematic Universe films.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:42.550
That's the same number as Iron Man and one
more than everybody's favorite Boy Scout,

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:43.220
Captain America.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:48.020
Following the wild success of Joss Whedon's
The Avengers, Marvel began to plot its storytelling

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:50.100
much more carefully than it had before.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:54.190
With the this recalibration, Marvel decided
to make the Infinity Stones the central story

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:55.980
elements of Phases 1 through 3.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:59.860
As a result, the Tesseract was retconned to
contain the Space Stone.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:04.240
This pivot towards the Infinity Stones as
the binding agent of the MCU will go down

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:07.860
in Hollywood history as one of the greatest
production moves of all time.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:11.830
And with a storyline more than 10 years in
the making finally coming to a close with

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.620
Endgame, it may indeed prove to be the end
of an era.

